  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decreasing anthropogenic disturbance in the Cao Vit Gibbon Conservation Area</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to assure the survival of the last remaining population of Cao Vit gibbons by reducing anthropogenic disturbance within the Cao Vit Gibbon Conservation Area. This will be done by: 1) replacing 9 wooden water wheels with steel water wheels in the 3 communes around the CVGCA; 2) presenting a training course on the sustainable harvesting of fuel wood for the 3 communes around the protected area; 3) conducting a village training course on cultivation of elephant grass and providing seedlings and fertilizer to introduce the plant to all three communes around the protected area; 4) conducting a goat buy-back scheme; 5) erecting 10 new and repairing 10 old protected area boundary markers; 6) constructing livestock exclusion fences on the protected area boundary at the most commonly used access points; 7) repairing 3 existing gibbon information boards and erecting 3 new ones in local villages; and 8) producing and distributing to local communes 1000 calendars using photographs of the Cao Vit gibbon and project activities.</narrative>
  </description>
